T[3621]=dict(
title="Sahara Desert Trek: Walking with Camels from M'Hamid",
ov=["Four days walking in the Sahara with a camel caravan, far from roads and towns. From M'Hamid El Ghizlane we follow dry riverbeds and cross big dunes. At night we sleep in nomad tents under more stars than you have ever seen.",
    "The walking is easy, about five hours a day, and the camels carry the bags. You can also ride a camel for a while if your feet need a rest. On the way there and back you cross the High Atlas and visit the Draa oasis and Ait Ben Haddou."],
facts=[("Tour name","Moroccan Sahara Desert Trek"),("Duration","8 days"),("Grade","Easy"),("Best time to visit","September to May"),("Type of travel","Trekking"),("Group size","Usually 2 to 16 people"),("Recommended age","8 to 75"),("Start / finish","Marrakech"),("Accommodation","Hotel or riad, and desert camps during the trek")],
inc=["Meals: 7 breakfasts, 7 lunches and 6 dinners, plus water during the trek","Accommodation: 3 nights in hotels and 4 nights in camps","Transport by comfortable van or Toyota 4x4","A visit to the old medina of Marrakech, 4 days of trekking in the Sahara, a tour of Ait Ben Haddou and a camel ride in the desert"],
exc=["Flights","Visas","Meals not listed in the itinerary","Tips, drinks, laundry and souvenirs","Personal travel insurance"],
hl=["Explore the medina of Marrakech","Cross the High Atlas Mountains","Visit the film studios of Ouarzazate","See Ait Ben Haddou, a famous film location","Trek through the Sahara with camels","Visit the Draa oasis"],
it={1:("Arrival in Marrakech","Welcome to Marrakech, the Red City. Look for the We Gravel Morocco sign at Menara Airport, and we'll drive you to your hotel. Explore the city if you like before the welcome meeting, where you meet your guide and go through the trip."),
2:("Marrakech to M'Hamid and the Draa oasis","A long but beautiful drive today. We cross the High Atlas over the Tizi n'Tichka pass (2,260 m), the highest road pass in Morocco. We stop for lunch in the big palm groves of the Draa Valley, then continue to Ras Nkhal on the edge of the Sahara. First night in camp."),
3:("Oulad Driss to Sidi Naji","The trek begins. Once the camels are loaded, we walk through golden dunes to the big dune of Erg Mado and climb it for a wide view over the desert. Lunch is a picnic in the shade of tamarisk trees. Night in camp."),
4:("Sidi Naji to Erg Zahar","We follow the camels across stony plateaus and climb the dune of Erg Zahar for another great view. Night in camp."),
5:("Erg Zahar to Erg Smar","Get up early for the sunrise and have breakfast in the open air. Then we walk deeper into the desert along the dry bed of the Draa River. You can ride a camel for a while, and the camel men will show you how they bake bread in the hot sand. Night in camp."),
6:("Erg Smar to Oulad Driss, transfer to Agdz","After breakfast we walk for an hour and a half to Oulad Driss and say goodbye to the caravan team. Then we drive to the Agdz oasis and spend the night in a kasbah."),
7:("Agdz to Marrakech via Ait Ben Haddou","We follow the old caravan road through a green oasis to Ait Ben Haddou, the ksar used in many films. After lunch we walk through the old village, then drive on to Marrakech."),
8:("Departure","Transfer to the airport for your flight home.")})
T[3616]=dict(
title="Climb Mount Toubkal: 6-Day Trek from Marrakech",
ov=["Toubkal (4,167 m) is the highest mountain in Morocco and in North Africa. This 6-day trip takes the quieter route to the top, over the Tizi Mzik and Aguelzim passes, through Toubkal National Park and past Berber villages and high valleys.",
    "Before and after the trek you have time in Marrakech, with a guided tour of its palaces, gardens, souks and Jemaa el-Fna square. The trip ends with a farewell dinner."],
facts=[("Tour name","Climb Mount Toubkal"),("Duration","6 days, 5 nights, 3 days of trekking"),("Grade","Moderate to hard"),("Best time to visit","March to November"),("Type of travel","Trekking"),("Group size","2 to 16 people"),("Recommended age","18 to 75"),("Start / finish","Marrakech"),("Accommodation","Guesthouse, camp and riad")],
inc=["Meals: 5 breakfasts, 4 lunches and 5 dinners, plus mineral water during the trek","Accommodation: 2 nights in a riad, 1 night in a guesthouse and 2 nights in camps","Transport: airport transfer, Marrakech to Imlil and back by comfortable van or 4x4, plus mules and muleteers during the trek","The guided climb of Toubkal and a guided tour of Marrakech"],
exc=["Flights","Visas","Meals not listed in the itinerary","Tips, drinks, laundry and souvenirs","Personal travel insurance"],
hl=["Explore the lanes of the old medina of Marrakech","See how Berber families live in the mountains","Climb the highest mountain in North Africa","Farewell dinner with live music and oriental dance"],
it={1:("Arrival in Marrakech","Welcome to Marrakech, the Red City. Look for the We Gravel Morocco sign at Menara Airport, and we'll drive you to your riad. Explore the city if you like, then meet the group and your guide to go through the trip."),
2:("Marrakech (450 m) to Azib Tamsoult (2,400 m)","After breakfast we drive to Imlil and meet the muleteers. We walk up to the Tizi Mzik pass (2,450 m) and have lunch with a view over the Imnan valley. Then we continue to Azib Tamsoult and camp for the night."),
3:("Azib Tamsoult to the Aguelzim pass (3,550 m) and the Toubkal refuge (3,207 m)","A steady climb on an old mule path brings us to the Aguelzim pass, with a superb view of the Toubkal massif. After a picnic we go down to the refuge and camp for the night."),
4:("Toubkal summit (4,167 m) and Aremd (1,900 m)","Summit day. We start early and reach the top in about three and a half hours. On a clear day you can see for miles in every direction. After some time on the summit we go back down to the refuge for lunch, then continue to Aremd for a night in a guesthouse."),
5:("Aremd to Imlil and Marrakech","A short walk down the valley brings us back to Imlil, where the trek ends. We drive to Marrakech, and after lunch you have a guided tour of the city's mosques, palaces and gardens. Then you're free to explore until the farewell dinner."),
6:("Departure","Transfer to the airport, depending on your flight time.")})
T[3611]=dict(
title="Classic Toubkal Trek: 3 Days from Marrakech",
ov=["This is the classic Toubkal trek, and the quickest way to stand on the roof of North Africa. In three days you walk from Imlil up through Berber villages and a rocky high valley to the summit of Toubkal (4,167 m), then back down again.",
    "It's hard work but not technical. Mules carry the bags, and you sleep one night at the base camp and one in a village guesthouse. If you're short on time but want a real mountain, this is the trip for you."],
facts=[("Tour name","Classic Toubkal Climb"),("Duration","3 days, 2 nights"),("Grade","Moderate to hard"),("Best time to visit","March to November"),("Type of travel","Trekking"),("Group size","2 to 16 people"),("Recommended age","16 to 70"),("Start / finish","Marrakech or Imlil"),("Accommodation","Guesthouse and camp")],
inc=["Meals: 2 breakfasts, 2 lunches and 2 dinners, plus mineral water during the trek","Accommodation: 1 night in a guesthouse and 1 night in a camp","Transport by comfortable van or 4x4, plus mules and muleteers during the trek","The guided climb of Toubkal"],
exc=["Flights","Visas","Meals not listed in the itinerary","Tips, drinks, laundry and souvenirs","Personal travel insurance"],
hl=["Climb Toubkal (4,167 m), the highest peak in North Africa","Walk through traditional Berber villages","Explore Marrakech before or after the trek"],
it={1:("Marrakech to Imlil (1,750 m) and the Toubkal base camp (3,207 m)","We pick you up from your hotel or riad in Marrakech and drive about an hour and a half to Imlil. There you meet the muleteers and start a five-hour walk to the base camp. We pass the village of Aremd (1,950 m) and stop for lunch at the shrine of Sidi Chamharouch (2,360 m), then zigzag up to the base camp. You sleep in the refuge, or in a tent if you prefer, from May to the end of October."),
2:("Toubkal summit (4,167 m) and Aremd (1,900 m)","We start early for the summit of Toubkal, the highest point in the Atlas and in North Africa. From the top, the views stretch across the Atlas toward the Sahara. We go back down to the refuge for lunch, then continue to Aremd for the night."),
3:("Aremd to Marrakech","After breakfast at the guesthouse we walk down to Imlil and drive about an hour and a half back to Marrakech, arriving around midday. Add a guided tour of the medina if you'd like to see more of the city.")})
T[3606]=dict(
title="Climb Mount M'Goun (4,071 m): 8-Day Trek",
ov=["M'Goun (4,071 m) is the second-highest mountain in North Africa, and much quieter than Toubkal. On this 8-day trek you walk up from the green Ait Bouguemez valley, cross passes above 3,400 m, follow old nomad paths and camp on high plateaus before the summit day.",
    "The route is wild and varied. You see green fields, Berber villages, deep valleys and open high mountains. On the way in and out you also visit the natural bridge of Imi n'Ifri and the Ouzoud waterfalls."],
facts=[("Tour name","Mount M'Goun Trek"),("Duration","8 days, 7 nights, 5 days of trekking"),("Grade","Moderate to hard"),("Best time to visit","June to October"),("Type of travel","Trekking"),("Group size","2 to 16 people"),("Recommended age","18 to 80"),("Start / finish","Marrakech"),("Accommodation","Guesthouse, camps and a hotel or riad")],
inc=["Meals: 7 breakfasts, 6 lunches and 6 dinners, plus mineral water during the trek","Accommodation: 2 nights in a hotel, 1 night in a guesthouse and 4 nights in camps","Transport by comfortable van or 4x4, plus mules and muleteers during the trek","The guided climb of M'Goun"],
exc=["Flights and visas","Meals not listed in the itinerary","Tips, drinks, laundry and souvenirs","Personal travel insurance"],
hl=["Visit the imperial city of Marrakech","Hike through remote high-mountain landscapes","Climb the second-highest peak in North Africa","Walk on old nomad paths","See the natural bridge of Imi n'Ifri","Visit the Ouzoud waterfalls"],
it={1:("Arrival in Marrakech","Your driver meets you at Menara Airport and takes you to your hotel. In the late afternoon your mountain guide briefs you on the trek, and in the evening you sit down to your first Moroccan dinner."),
2:("Marrakech to the Ait Bouguemez valley via Imi n'Ifri","We leave the city behind and drive to the foothills of the central High Atlas. On the way we stop at Imi n'Ifri, a natural limestone bridge carved by the river that still flows under it. We have a picnic after a short walk across the bridge, then drive up into the hidden Ait Bouguemez valley. After mint tea with the muleteers, we walk up the Arous gorge to the pastures of Azib n'Ikiss (2,250 m) and camp for the night."),
3:("Ikiss (2,250 m) to the Tarkdit plateau (2,900 m)","The bags go on the mules and we climb steadily for about three hours to the Aghouri pass (3,400 m), with our first view of the M'Goun summit. After a slow picnic we follow a nomad path down to the Tarkdit plateau and camp."),
4:("M'Goun summit (4,071 m) to Oulilimt (2,600 m)","The big day. The climb isn't technical but the trail is steep, and it's a long, tough mountain day. From the top the view takes in the High Atlas, the Anti-Atlas and the Rose Valley. We go down to the Oulilimt valley to camp.<br><strong>Note:</strong> If you'd rather skip the summit, you can walk with the muleteers to the next camp, an easier walk of about 5–6 hours."),
5:("Oulilimt (2,600 m) to Ain Aflafal (2,300 m)","We start by going down to Tighramt, below M'Goun, then walk an easy five hours through the wild Oulilimt valley to Ain Aflafal, with a picnic by the river on the way. Night in camp at Tighramt n'Ait Hemd."),
6:("Ain Aflafal (2,300 m) to Tabant (2,000 m)","We head back to the Happy Valley over the Tizi n'Ait Imi pass (2,900 m). The 550 m climb is rewarded with a great view over the M'Goun range. After a picnic at the pass, a 950 m descent brings us to Tabant, the main village of the valley and the end of the trek. Night in a guesthouse."),
7:("Tabant to Marrakech via Azilal and the Ouzoud waterfalls","We say goodbye to the trekking team and drive back to Marrakech via Azilal and the Ouzoud waterfalls. You reach your hotel in the early afternoon, with time to visit the medina and Jemaa el-Fna square before the farewell dinner."),
8:("Departure","Transfer to the airport, depending on your flight time.")})
